      "problem": "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find $2r+s.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply each component of $r$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2r+s & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12+(-6) \\\\ 10+3 \\\\ 0+7 \\\\ 12+(-8) \\\\ 4+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
